# Production vs artifacts

| Kind | Location |
|------|----------|
| Production code | `src/` |
| Production tests | `tests/` |
| Permanent docs (explicitly accepted only) | `docs/` |
| Experiments, benches, audits, generated reports, prototypes | `.artifacts/` |

If unsure a document is permanent: write it under `.artifacts/`. Never default to `docs/SOMETHING.md`.

Do not put experimental/benchmark/prototype/diagnostic code under `src/`, `tests/`, `docs/`, or `tools/` unless the user explicitly promotes it.

Promotion (`.artifacts/` → `docs/` or `src/`/`tests/`) requires an explicit user decision.

## Source of truth

1. Current `src/`
2. Current `tests/`
3. Accepted `docs/`
4. `.artifacts/` (historical evidence only)

Before command or data-plane work: inspect production code, then `.artifacts/ARTIFACT-INDEX.md`, then relevant artifacts. Do not treat an old report as current architecture.

Policy: `.artifacts/REPOSITORY-ARTIFACT-POLICY.md`.

Do not delete or “clean up” historical artifacts. Do not implement features or optimize as part of indexing/hygiene tasks.
